==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To put (food) on to a dish ready for eating.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To distribute (a thing).
# {{lb|en|transitive|figuratively}} To distribute or deliver something.
#: ''She can '''dish out''' criticism but she can't take it.''
# {{lb|en|transitive|architecture}} To [[hollow out]], as a gutter in stone or wood.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|food}} {{l|en|dish up}}, {{l|en|serve}}
* {{sense|distribute}} {{l|en|distribute}}, {{l|en|give out}}, {{l|en|hand out}}, {{l|en|hand round}}, {{l|en|pass out}}, {{l|en|pass round}}
* {{sense|figuratively}} {{l|en|give out}}

